bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:09a26ef78a2ae6c6afb158708a41a9dd478a77c52d8538109895ed69975b77a9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0ad75c1247de1bd512dfd84a486a2570b29dec617cba08279b7df25ba46880ec by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0e3c14f0268962766b2c8239747b7bb6057027d30df8278561f8e05ce767be91 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0e3c14f0268962766b2c8239747b7bb6057027d30df8278561f8e05ce767be91 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The object, with the cases it has to pass before any code is written for it.\nA cell is two poles on a lattice it is given, never a lattice it assumes: the same cell folds over an interval, an alphabet and a ladder, and the state it is in is the one that lattice names.\nA signature narrows a bound and every cell resting on that bound reads the narrower one; no origin's claim is edited by it, and the order signatures arrive in never shows.\nA withdrawal names the claim it takes back, not a value that looks like it, and fold by phase adds claims at one turn of the period as the square of their number.\nAll four corners are reached: one origin that pins a level is REQUIRED, two that leave the scale open are FREE, two that touch under a ceiling below the top are FORBIDDEN, and two that cannot both hold are CONFLICT.\nThe object, written down once: two poles read at a resolution, origins that carry the epoch they spoke at and a sign, and an order of rest against other cells.\nFive operations answer for it and there are no others. Meet is what the origins hold together, encounter is how many met and what that makes, observe is one more origin at a cost, sign is a bound narrowed wherever it is rested on, refine is the same cell read at another resolution.\nA withdrawal takes back its own write and nothing else, so a cell that was written and withdrawn at one epoch is a cell nobody claimed.\nEight acts in four pairs answer for it under seven names, each an offer with a descriptor, and what a descriptor forces is derived from it and refused: a widening that travels, a floor required past a signed ceiling, a withdrawal that leaves its pole where the claim put it, and an order of rest that returns to itself."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0e400f61b310f502c517d8806c0c28c4b1a7e0edbdb3e5c6261513b69726ac2e by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0e400f61b310f502c517d8806c0c28c4b1a7e0edbdb3e5c6261513b69726ac2e by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Bits of freedom are what is left to decide in a cell: log2 of the states between the floor it requires and the ceiling it permits — the states in the upset of the floor that are also in the downset of the ceiling. A decided cell has none, and a cell in conflict has none either: no state satisfies it.\nResolution is chain length: on a chain the states between are an interval of it; on any lattice they are the interval [floor, ceiling] of its order."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0eeec250ea70dd5c425119c9f7be59864d51c3946d7d7063fe31cfdba47cfb81 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0eeec250ea70dd5c425119c9f7be59864d51c3946d7d7063fe31cfdba47cfb81 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The debit as a vector: four states per irreducible, and the counter is the\npopcount of one of them. Two bits compose; four labels do not, which is why\nthe state is derived and never stored.\n\nThe alphabet cases enumerate a five-token palette against every interesting\npair of (demanded, permitted). The interval cases are runs: the answer only\nchanges where a boundary is, so a million values cost the same as five."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:0fec7ebdf38cd943e237a6b534d81639aca0530fa6057419c8efaa6e026e2fe6 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:10281a8210f93e12f2837d9bd661d44695a8d7c74547aa5bcd39e4888f208b44 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:10281a8210f93e12f2837d9bd661d44695a8d7c74547aa5bcd39e4888f208b44 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Two hundred thousand cells resting on one root: a wide signature, a tighter one, and the tighter taken back, each one line at the root; a thousand cells probed."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:113a60882006d0d3a2f080856f3efa7992fe56f6295a7e128480299b283e99eb by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:113a60882006d0d3a2f080856f3efa7992fe56f6295a7e128480299b283e99eb by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T88, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:11efb17ae6505fd9a7d3a3749b36522eebdec428b23ef2c45952d31f2453ae23 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:11efb17ae6505fd9a7d3a3749b36522eebdec428b23ef2c45952d31f2453ae23 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="prop-dep on a product of two subsystems: both costs decompose into the factors plus what the joint says over them.\nThe conflict carries the dependence of the demand less that of the meet; the premium carries the residual information of the dependence itself.\nPinned at the crossed declaration and at (everything demanded, nothing permitted); the identities are checked at all sixteen."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:13a02d4eb5c8eac1a51552564d9f1a086996c083aeaa5a771cf05699be57e037 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:13a02d4eb5c8eac1a51552564d9f1a086996c083aeaa5a771cf05699be57e037 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="One origin of one width is worth what it connects: nothing inside a city where every pair already had a walk, one pair between two lone cells, and the product of two components when it lands across a desert.\nThe same claim, the same cost, four placements and four prices, so where to look is a question with an answer.\nWhat it crosses is named before it lands."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1475fc605a499644ba2adadfd4650d62dffddc59195314f1ae4d302a4d191029 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1475fc605a499644ba2adadfd4650d62dffddc59195314f1ae4d302a4d191029 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A pair splits over the blocks of its meet: each block carries its own residual information, weighted by its share of the places.\nInside a block the restricted pair has a trivial meet, so the sum is bounded by the largest a trivial meet can reach.\nChecked at every pair of the partition lattice on four places."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1645289e45ce7d30d5b6182d269d7d8f5056eaed6d994b3e35837a3a4c7320b5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:181e4540535a619fa99f1071935524b0a9fa42b9f29702328e0a534ca825a3ff by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:181e4540535a619fa99f1071935524b0a9fa42b9f29702328e0a534ca825a3ff by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The observer is a cell: its floor no look, its ceiling thirty; five looks later its ceiling is twenty-five.\nIts reach over fifteen cells is where its region meets theirs."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:182877c309289a87e6bed99a81b452ab608e451b45b34f44485167d3d87d26a5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:182877c309289a87e6bed99a81b452ab608e451b45b34f44485167d3d87d26a5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T87, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:186fada24a1aae859b0fde6415a890f400895a8dedbef890225f0f2a3f8079da by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|brief|cases|title
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:186fada24a1aae859b0fde6415a890f400895a8dedbef890225f0f2a3f8079da by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Where reading already is, the next reading lands: origins placed in proportion to the origins a cell already carries.\nOver eight epochs the ratio between the densest tenth and the sparsest tenth rises at every epoch and the deserts stay empty.\nThe same budget of origins placed without regard to density holds that ratio near two and touches three times as many cells."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:186fada24a1aae859b0fde6415a890f400895a8dedbef890225f0f2a3f8079da by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/brief value="reading lands where reading already is"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:186fada24a1aae859b0fde6415a890f400895a8dedbef890225f0f2a3f8079da by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/title value="Density attracts"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:18c0a71e8f1ab0481b746125eb2de33f67b6886ee672270e0c14a9f05ad1f3f1 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:18c0a71e8f1ab0481b746125eb2de33f67b6886ee672270e0c14a9f05ad1f3f1 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A lock is mostly settled. Of the claims standing on this tree, the form of most leaves them one legal state: they are applied, and nothing about them is open.\nWhat the form leaves with more than one state splits again: a reading closes some, some stand in force with nothing yet read against them, and a few say of themselves that they are decisions and are the only ones open.\nThe four classes are a partition: every claim is in exactly one, and their sizes fall in that order, most settled first."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a7c6479ae724ce8238ca9469cf6dd2286eea4a9326c6fd61abc4496adefe36d by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases|coverage|family|note
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/lang value=ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/specifiers value=../debit/ideal.ts|../debit/provenance.ts|../debit/unit-span.ts|../debit/unit.ts|../field/field.ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/answers value="how finely a cell is resolved and how it moves along its scale"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/head value="\n * The lattice as a chain, or read along its chains: resolution is chain length. It answers how finely a cell is\n * resolved and how it moves along its scale: its state among the four, how two units compose, and the runs and\n * transitions of a vector of them.\n *\n * Which operation answers this view is read off the laws its vectors fix: the view an operation has is the view of\n * the laws that name the vectors it ran on, or of the definition it implements. An operation no law reaches keeps the\n * view it was given by hand, as drift. Nothing here is new algebra: every name is re-exported once.\n "
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/customised value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/dynamic value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/lexed value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/lines value=14..14
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/longest value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1a902c71b5fc998478edc3c2fa7991bbfa6bb1233f6325430227cbaab9f20622 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1aaed8bb355933beafdafbcecaaddd3bd33b985616dec610c29bd6b77f55cfe1 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases|chain|coverage|empty|family|note
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1b270dc0ca7b5a25fe88562fdf65e950829cb71c26f6f9035562bb8b50ee712a by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage|powerset
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1b270dc0ca7b5a25fe88562fdf65e950829cb71c26f6f9035562bb8b50ee712a by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="meetBlocks groups the join-irreducibles of [u ^ w, u v w] by COMPARABILITY,\nand priceByBlocks prices each group. This is the localisation pair.\n\nOn a chain every irreducible is comparable to every other, so there is always\nexactly ONE block: a case built only on a chain cannot tell a correct\npartition from any other.\n\nAnd every obvious valuation — index, index squared — is SUPERMODULAR, and\nmonotone with supermodular gives g = 0. A file built from those alone reports\nzero premiums everywhere while looking thorough. `pricesAnything` exists to\nsay so: the runner calls it, and a case claiming a premium on a valuation\nthat prices nothing is refused.\n\nWhich lattices have anything to localise:\n\n  A BLOCK CONTRIBUTES A NON-ZERO PREMIUM ONLY IF THE SUBLATTICE IT GENERATES\n  CONTAINS AN INCOMPARABLE PAIR — for a MONOTONE INCREASING valuation, which\n  is the shape a design scale has, since worth rises with level. There\n  `priceByBlocks` returns 0 on all 81 pairs of a 9-rung chain, and the\n  spectrum collapses to {0}.\n\nThe condition is monotone, not every. A DECREASING valuation gives a non-zero\npremium in 79 of those 81 pairs and a sawtooth one in 62. And `premium` and\n`gap` are two quantities rather than one: on the same chain `gap` is 0 in\n81/81 for an increasing valuation and non-zero in 64/81 for a decreasing one.\n\nRI <= 0 does not license `g == 0` on its own. Monotone AND supermodular gives\nzero counterexamples while either half alone leaves many, and among MONOTONE\nvaluations `g != 0` iff not supermodular, exactly. `pricesAnything` carries\nboth halves; `!isSupermodular` is IDENTICALLY FALSE on a chain, so a runner\nthat checks only that half passes vacuously.\n\nB2 and M3 fall there for the plainest reason available: all their\njoin-irreducibles are atoms, so every pair meets at bottom, so every block is\na singleton, so every block generates the 2-chain {bottom, x}. Add a STEM —\none level between bottom and the atoms — and the atoms meet above bottom, the\nblock has something to price, and the localised total reconciles exactly.\nThat pair of cases is below, and it is what makes this a theorem rather than\na shrug.\n\nA board that is a PRODUCT OF SCALES has its irreducibles only on the axes, so\ntwo from different axes meet at bottom, so the blocks ARE the axes and each\naxis is a chain. `priceByBlocks` is therefore identically zero on a product\nof chains. B2 and M3 are not pathological corners; they are the smallest\nmembers of that family."
