bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1c6575d3da8408a109707b7e087437f4c9310b954eff4dac02245d9496e92878 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:1c6575d3da8408a109707b7e087437f4c9310b954eff4dac02245d9496e92878 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="How much worse a plain retreat can be than the cheapest one, over every declaration in conflict on the partition lattice.\nThe worst is a demand of two balanced blocks, and it is exactly what the block sizes predict.\nIt is half the places for an even number of them, and a little under for an odd one."
