bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:3dcc2df90473ce16a3cc1fa38d0e7681e6f2e14d11e08bc83445fc7b14192acc by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T99, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:3fa82ad52b46f66e90b4a7bee2bcfbc7e94fb9634dfc822266cde24199283bdd by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:3fa82ad52b46f66e90b4a7bee2bcfbc7e94fb9634dfc822266cde24199283bdd by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A lock and a target are one object: a span. What may be and what must be fold by the same meet, split by the same\ndisagreement, and a value stands against both exactly when it stands in their meet. The algebra has no roles."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:401ac44d568cdf42592e2975e5fe24269893fb2a76d8dc19b61940a3b19b90e2 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:401ac44d568cdf42592e2975e5fe24269893fb2a76d8dc19b61940a3b19b90e2 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The context of Birkhoff: for each join-irreducible j, the\nmeet-irreducibles m with j ≤ m. Both cards of a debit are derived\nfrom this table. A file that only checked a chain would hide that\nthe two faces are different sets — on a chain they look like shifts\nof each other.\n\nThe trap: treating joins() as the old debits() (JI only) and never\nlooking at limits()."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:425a76ea0babe65f3a0c40d491d8775c30410bd16ac54239c050e2924da1070b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:425a76ea0babe65f3a0c40d491d8775c30410bd16ac54239c050e2924da1070b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The quarter turn read three ways over a grid of phase pairs: the cancel test, the summed intensity below two, and the angle beyond π/2.\nPhases drawn at σ = π/(2·0.6745·√2), where half the differences on the line exceed a quarter turn since 0.6745 is the median of a unit normal's size; counted by the quarter turn, which wraps, fewer pairs cancel, and one coherence stays laminar at that spread and below it."
