bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:43ef0a5c1abcf87f2e4aef388f728dcb7df74d2e0bf8351177cb860e0304251b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:43ef0a5c1abcf87f2e4aef388f728dcb7df74d2e0bf8351177cb860e0304251b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Merging two blocks costs at least two, and exactly two only when both are single places.\nSo coarsening a reading by one block costs at least two, every time.\nChecked on every pair of block sizes that fits in six places, and on every coarsening in the partition lattice on four."
