bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:5671d8010ca4a5ab79cdc700d5b665dcef6b4de80e732c773741401463056343 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/lines value=80..80
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:5671d8010ca4a5ab79cdc700d5b665dcef6b4de80e732c773741401463056343 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/longest value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:5671d8010ca4a5ab79cdc700d5b665dcef6b4de80e732c773741401463056343 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:568ee9aedf201cab16cb7bc8a124492249f9ce2ab2748a4ffefa2a95001261a4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:568ee9aedf201cab16cb7bc8a124492249f9ce2ab2748a4ffefa2a95001261a4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The field is the lattice and the debit in motion. Each origin at a point holds a band on a scale — the floor it demands, the ceiling it allows — and the point's declaration is their fold: the demand is the join of the floors, the limit the meet of the ceilings.\nA point's state is one of the debit's four, and green, grey, red and fork are its renders (FREE, REQUIRED, FORBIDDEN, CONFLICT). The register read at the point gives every debit's state; a declaration is in conflict exactly when some debit is (the debit).\nThe premium of the point's declaration is the gap; under a supermodular valuation it vanishes on every declaration. A region withdraws exactly when its scale is distributive. What moved between two readings is counted debit by debit.\nNothing here is new algebra: every reading is an operation of lattice/ or debit/ applied to a point of field/."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:575661fb3bb6ca2a41e2776b4e2c6226efb9e1913c27bea2f39844a43f512084 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/lang value=ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:575661fb3bb6ca2a41e2776b4e2c6226efb9e1913c27bea2f39844a43f512084 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/specifiers value=../debit/debit.ts|../field/encounter.ts|../field/field.ts|../field/join.ts|../field/meet.ts|../field/observe.ts|../field/refine.ts|../field/require.ts|../field/sign.ts|../field/present.ts|./field/wave.ts|../lattice/obligatory.ts|../debit/observer.ts|./field/physics.ts|./field/policy.ts|./field/self.ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:575661fb3bb6ca2a41e2776b4e2c6226efb9e1913c27bea2f39844a43f512084 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/answers value="where a bound is held and by whom"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:575661fb3bb6ca2a41e2776b4e2c6226efb9e1913c27bea2f39844a43f512084 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/head value="\n * The lattice laid over coordinates: every bound is held somewhere, at a resolution and an epoch, by origins. It\n * answers where a bound is held and by whom: what met there, whether the origins agree, what the present is, and what\n * a replay of everything that landed folds to.\n *\n * Which operation answers this view is read off the laws its vectors fix: the view an operation has is the view of\n * the laws that name the vectors it ran on, or of the definition it implements. An operation no law reaches keeps the\n * view it was given by hand, as drift. Nothing here is new algebra: every name is re-exported once.\n "
