bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:57cdea4f0c7b44b954a8d1dcdbf0df0b432f046ad3e4de7c31d54591cf0e9cf7 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:58fb6c7d3612cc22f4d970d9dc99e3e00068cdb144539fe03902ecadbb54737f by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage|turned
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:58fb6c7d3612cc22f4d970d9dc99e3e00068cdb144539fe03902ecadbb54737f by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A point is a place where origins can coincide: its state is the set of origins that touched it, with the span each\none holds. \"Has a second origin\", \"where do they disagree\" and \"what turned\" are reads of that set at the point,\nnever a join over a key somebody chose: the coordinate is the key (L00), and an encounter is two origins in one\nplace (L01).\n\nIt got its own file because reconciliation is an industry: with relations stored and coincidence searched afterwards,\nasking whether two origins saw one thing costs a pass over everything; here it costs reading one set."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:598c1c48a98f9d2c6387197176f2383b378deb02697ef9084067e82b1c49c086 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:59994a1491ddf71d59f56464f7b45902a8cc26dfb9796f476a5fc9f2636b0b09 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|brief|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:59994a1491ddf71d59f56464f7b45902a8cc26dfb9796f476a5fc9f2636b0b09 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The falsifier: one act that is both local and non-local — a change that travels a distance and also reaches a cell that does not rest on its bound. The two poles would then be one, and this would be a claim about the world rather than a hint."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:59994a1491ddf71d59f56464f7b45902a8cc26dfb9796f476a5fc9f2636b0b09 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/brief value="one act is both local and non-local"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:59b8536141af25813eaa08a7e0b3e7657450a69c6dcaa3aa285ca03be6922769 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:59b8536141af25813eaa08a7e0b3e7657450a69c6dcaa3aa285ca03be6922769 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A valuation is supermodular when RI ≤ 0 on every pair. Monotone and\nsupermodular gives g ≡ 0: planning is worth nothing. Height on a modular lattice\nis modular, hence supermodular. A cheap join on B2 is not.\n\nThe trap: checking only chains, where every monotone function of\nrank is supermodular because there are no incomparable pairs."
