bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:6b1c1819904fcb9acb1e345ae01485625731e2b686113dec25d93c519c834f20 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:6b1c1819904fcb9acb1e345ae01485625731e2b686113dec25d93c519c834f20 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The rule that makes the game is in the field and not above it: a cell one origin has claimed is grey, and nothing that origin does alone will close it.\nTwenty cells each with one origin, and no look at all, close nothing and cover nothing. Forty looks by another origin close fifteen and cover every cell.\nSo what an origin is worth is asymmetric — nothing over its own claims, everything over another's — and the referee is the rule itself, which no player can suspend."
