bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:92a4518c769f9ab2d168d4b6a9ef1da63ff8d666ac0215718e6f00e52701fe2a by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|chain|coverage|sideBySide
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:92a4518c769f9ab2d168d4b6a9ef1da63ff8d666ac0215718e6f00e52701fe2a by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would have to change for `have` to reach `want`.\n\nA LIST on each side, because there can be more than one weakest answer.\nEmpty means that side already holds. On a plain ladder there is always\nexactly one, so every case here has at most a single entry — the\nambiguous case needs a scale where two levels sit side by side, and that\nis the side-by-side case below.\n\nThe weakest answer is not `higher(have, want)`. That one works and is not\nthe smallest, which only shows up off a ladder."
