bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a901e2ff834faf5bee059c0d65c289b5c6056999aedfd5fad05197dc607a21a1 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a90bcf19973176f3f2781c409f4b9fa9571a4fb22ffdfe8b7b31b1952aa557a7 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage|crossed
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a90bcf19973176f3f2781c409f4b9fa9571a4fb22ffdfe8b7b31b1952aa557a7 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="viol* and the premium g = viol − viol*. On a chain, g is identically\nzero for any monotone valuation — planning is worth nothing, the\nretreat is already optimal. Off a chain it need not be.\n\nThe trap: reporting gated = coarse − gain as the optimum. That equals\nviol* only under collapse (g = RI). The square-by-index valuation on\nB2 has g = 0 and RI = −4 at (x, y), so gated is not best."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a94bd146f1237ad789fe84d52ea8af8de9b3591b4fa12d06162b99fbff44ba9e by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a94bd146f1237ad789fe84d52ea8af8de9b3591b4fa12d06162b99fbff44ba9e by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T94, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a96e4689e68e808d844f8b3679f0392ceb40132e7311d71822a8d1cce06b8e48 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a96e4689e68e808d844f8b3679f0392ceb40132e7311d71822a8d1cce06b8e48 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The inputs the other six files never send.\n\nEvery other vector file is well-formed on purpose, and that turned out to\nbe a blind spot with a shape: a duplicated level name made `rank` return\none of two indices — same input, two answers — and that broke\n`pack`/`unpack` being inverse.\n\nWIDTH IS NOT HERE ON PURPOSE. An opinion holds as many debits as the host's\nbitwise word, and both refuse rather than truncate. A shared vector at\na width one past the opinion would fail a correct implementation."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a9f772fead233c24cac525223651c3dcb1affeec8781b5f9e90a1e673ed94f17 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:a9f772fead233c24cac525223651c3dcb1affeec8781b5f9e90a1e673ed94f17 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Information and distance are two readings of one thing: with no origin there is neither a fact nor a finite distance, and each origin that lands gives exactly one of each.\nThe scan runs the origins up from zero and the two counts move together at every step.\nSo the geometry is not a stage the knowing happens on; it is the shape the knowing takes."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:aa92d108eda875486fe8850835537286d552a78b2f7749cfac6ea31e3585ff6b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|chain|coordinatewise|coverage|states
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:aa92d108eda875486fe8850835537286d552a78b2f7749cfac6ea31e3585ff6b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The state of every step under one statement — the read-out that\ncomposes exactly.\n\nA single label per statement cannot: two cells of the four-by-four\nstay undecided by the labels alone. Each step carries two booleans\ninstead, and those combine independently.\n\nOnly the DEMAND side carries a state, so this walks the steps a\nstatement can demand — not the ones it can limit. An implementation\nwalking every level instead would produce one entry too many on a\nladder and get the bottom wrong.\n\nThe crossed case is the one that matters: a statement nothing can\nsatisfy still has a read-out, and CONFLICT appears step by step."
