bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b261226aaf93547b687ee06dc7b4de7490b0e917e0ad5a991c425caee0b91119 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b5c281bfba36b5dce72fd3b43b6105b8fb32d98bf8469a3d3cf0a9c3ee5defaa by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b5c281bfba36b5dce72fd3b43b6105b8fb32d98bf8469a3d3cf0a9c3ee5defaa by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Two signed values on one cell never replace each other. They relate by the cell's order:\nequal values are one encounter, the narrower value stands over the wider one, and\nincomparable values all stand as a fork that keeps both signers.\n\nIt got its own file because the first render of the owner's ledger kept the last line of\neach claim key and hid the rest by file order — ten keys on 2026-09-17, six of them\nre-signs that moved `needs` without withdrawing the old line.\n\n`standing` lists the member indices of every class left standing; an encounter keeps\nevery member, because no signature is overwritten."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b6a33d26d339b06007d0f65dcea7d19d5a8be925997efb2e5dd584cc43f9195b by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/lang value=ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/specifiers value=../debit/packed.ts|../debit/unit.ts
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/answers value="what can be taken back exactly"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=source/head value="\n * Complements: where the lattice is distributive every demand has one, and on the Boolean part of a scale truth is\n * functional. It answers what can be taken back exactly (a withdrawal loses nothing only where demands have\n * complements) and where a clash is a plain contradiction.\n *\n * Which operation answers this view is read off the laws its vectors fix: the view an operation has is the view of\n * the laws that name the vectors it ran on, or of the definition it implements. An operation no law reaches keeps the\n * view it was given by hand, as drift. Nothing here is new algebra: every name is re-exported once.\n "
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/customised value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b766e66af9016e18ddf17bce98b2f6e3571f4a4f4bf0b982e3519d8fdb1fae0b by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/dynamic value=0..0
