bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b7c7cf058222cbfc6949e2bb155ee4382188d9f9bc831fa850734d3def477fe5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases|coverage|family|note|readings
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b8236c5d9c60c976071eeb8779e4219f5c10c480c60520273a603ed81597ecff by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b8236c5d9c60c976071eeb8779e4219f5c10c480c60520273a603ed81597ecff by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The state at a coordinate is derivable from what landed there: equal values are one encounter shown by the latest\nlanding, a narrower value stands over a wider one, and values neither narrower nor wider stand together as a fork.\nThe order of landing changes which equal value is shown, never what stands."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b849fde1840fe7494f2b57c11213f8f100b3abc548fffbd48b57a8f6ec7cef5d by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b849fde1840fe7494f2b57c11213f8f100b3abc548fffbd48b57a8f6ec7cef5d by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="A deterministic shuffle, and the two ways one stops being a control.\n\nTHE FIRST is the closed form that cancels the salt:\n  j = (salt + i*17 + salt*i) % (i + 1)\nlooks salted, but salt + salt*i is salt*(i+1), which is zero modulo i+1.\nThe salt cancels identically, so sixty-four draws are ONE permutation drawn\nsixty-four times. `varies` is the case that catches it.\n\nTHE SECOND is the position-only rule, live until this vector existed:\n  j = (salt + i*17) % (i + 1)\ndoes not cancel, but j depends only on the position and the salt — never on\nthe data, never on a stream. Both call sites passed salt = 3, so there was\nexactly one null corpus, ever. And j collapses to 0 whenever i+1 divides 14.\n`degenerate` is that case, stated as the thing a shuffle must not be.\n\nAND THE LIMIT, which is not a bug in the shuffle but in what it is asked to\nfalsify: a permutation preserves the multiset exactly, so it cannot falsify\nany claim that is a function of the multiset alone — a floor, a ceiling, a\ncongruence, a concentration. Finding the law again on shuffled values is\nevidence the null was wrong, not that the law is false. `blind` pins the\nthree quantities that survive, so a miner can refuse to build a control that\nwould fire on the truth."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b86e03299dd60c0c83bb2f72a59ac2937ecaf4b5b7ffd6eba4a2b86f627082c3 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage|witness
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b86e03299dd60c0c83bb2f72a59ac2937ecaf4b5b7ffd6eba4a2b86f627082c3 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What is derived from points is not a new origin: a coarser reading of a point keeps exactly the origins\nit was read from, and what a region holds is the meet of its origins — never one more of them (L01)."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:b871a566a2964051886ae883f63eceac767822d2cabba0812e44fc598265b3ff by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases|coverage|family|note
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ba4ac0986f2467a226fb0be22a04c4e0ae362dd17b5af8a06ea161fd30ec9cbc by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ba4ac0986f2467a226fb0be22a04c4e0ae362dd17b5af8a06ea161fd30ec9cbc by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T85, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bbbc88d486fa42706bfa7ec29f0e57fcd58ae10492c207cb9a7706afe161f8c8 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|brief|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bbbc88d486fa42706bfa7ec29f0e57fcd58ae10492c207cb9a7706afe161f8c8 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The falsifier: a result of the usual formalism that cannot be stated with the four fields, or a prediction the restored fields make that the arithmetic forbids. This conjecture is about which structure is missing, not about numbers the arithmetic already gives."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bbbc88d486fa42706bfa7ec29f0e57fcd58ae10492c207cb9a7706afe161f8c8 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/brief value="the arithmetic forbids what the restored fields predict"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bc7f55ec544ce19fa4570f63d9b701545b3d6e7a73ff4796a2bbbb38e7bb06fe by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bc7f55ec544ce19fa4570f63d9b701545b3d6e7a73ff4796a2bbbb38e7bb06fe by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Curvature is not bought with origins: the same two hundred origins give a ratio near two when they land blind and above twenty when they land where reading already is.\nSo the shape of what is known is a fact about placement, not about budget, and it leaves cities and deserts in one field.\nNo cell ever carries an origin that was not placed in it."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bc9ed51bcfa9660a485919fdcee4d6784db8b8a4e1bfd6cabb407f22aa2ea0e0 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bc9ed51bcfa9660a485919fdcee4d6784db8b8a4e1bfd6cabb407f22aa2ea0e0 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="There is no after: what stands at a cell is what the latest epoch says, and the order the claims arrived in never decides.\nThree claims at three epochs, in every order they could have arrived, leave one reading."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:bfb3122c42b44ac96b686d9e9e26c2fccbdeaa50643592959c4fdef557ea5796 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/carries value=BoolView|DebitOutcome|Edge|Level|MeasureForm|Method|Scale|State|Unit|bottom|bottomIx|ceiling|floor|isLadder|isSimple|kind|levels|lost|subject|top|topIx|value
