bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d5730ccb0c8202b15c9baaec08ba5a640c306e7fece776abc3597b8aba4290b9 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=interval measure=count role=reads scope=source/unread value=0..0
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d66411a0c7a912ab96ff8adeb89705a0f9ba6f75b9a77f323c418c992a2c9df3 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d66411a0c7a912ab96ff8adeb89705a0f9ba6f75b9a77f323c418c992a2c9df3 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Two observers of one world hold their own origins, and their verdicts differ on the cells where one has looked and the other has not.\nThat is not a contradiction: wherever they hold the same origins at a cell they agree, every time.\nWhat a cell is depends on who is reading, and the disagreement is the difference of their horizons, never of the world."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d66c05e502c8d8f4d97379b0b12d6870f91dbff10586b4b24f0f1f40860bdfb5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|brief|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d66c05e502c8d8f4d97379b0b12d6870f91dbff10586b4b24f0f1f40860bdfb5 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The falsifier: a pair of the five operations whose composition the axioms do not determine. The join is already known to be absent from them: it does not travel, and naming what it is would be a second kind of arrow this conjecture does not have."
