bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d79332ada142dcb26bf6a2f1d683b9cf8d58645a0f3cd696b437dc2487880edb by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d79332ada142dcb26bf6a2f1d683b9cf8d58645a0f3cd696b437dc2487880edb by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T91, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d7cbb086bc32363c74d36da809c0a064c648bd332398ac40110b20334a87acaa by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d7cbb086bc32363c74d36da809c0a064c648bd332398ac40110b20334a87acaa by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The ways the object can be got wrong that no act's descriptor derives. A cell with no ceiling is not a cell; a meet that assumes the reals is a meet of one lattice pretending to be the meet; a state written as a word in the code is a state the lattice did not give. A signature that edits an origin's claim has forged a reading, and a withdrawal matched by value takes back a claim nobody made. And a floor raised by some composition of the other acts, taken in every order, would make require a second name for what was already there. What a descriptor forces is derived from the descriptors and run over every act, never written here: a widening that travels, narrows or lands with nobody standing for it, a travelling act that misses a cell resting on its bound, a narrowing that opens freedom, a pole stored, a withdrawal that does not restore."
