bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d937255cf6757b86313acfdb74f0cb712baff57bfbf62b01bda83a7527c39c58 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:d937255cf6757b86313acfdb74f0cb712baff57bfbf62b01bda83a7527c39c58 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="What would break T95, run against the object."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:da7a3c2ea2333825f05dba7f19ec81eac3b7510c1e887e2165f94050090a71fe by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:da7a3c2ea2333825f05dba7f19ec81eac3b7510c1e887e2165f94050090a71fe by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="An epoch is a phase: claims that arrive at the same turn of a period reinforce and claims half a period apart cancel.\nSweeping the delay of one half of the claims draws the fringe, and the pattern is the period's own shape, not the claims'.\nObserving one route — fixing when those claims arrived — moves the pattern to its complement."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:dbc2af6ceb3bd761052e4951df55c89d2ea35596c982646d6ac4fa8223fbcba9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:df5fb3c630e20c348e3f68a874fdcfbe0a3417e14b5d93b4ba9ec3297a8911e9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:df5fb3c630e20c348e3f68a874fdcfbe0a3417e14b5d93b4ba9ec3297a8911e9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="An observation has a close: what was read before the close is partial and stands for nothing; the readings at or\nafter it are the observation, and the latest of them is what stands at that coordinate."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e35425f61abab42865ae06ea052af32056b282d3a434690b0ccd9f856bb5ae9a by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e6a91765e875d5db3737f738725abd4d643f5bab984b149ae28d53e8cd48e3ca by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|chain|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e6a91765e875d5db3737f738725abd4d643f5bab984b149ae28d53e8cd48e3ca by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The vacuity checker names what a predicate does over the valuations it samples: it discriminates, with a witness on each side; it holds whatever the valuation; or it never reads one.\nThe predicates are code a file cannot hold; they are built beside the test, and this file names each by the verdict it must draw."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e6c422556cd7133e9f36ef5b820fbf806d48b709b8dba71c0ad54135e84ebbd4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e6c422556cd7133e9f36ef5b820fbf806d48b709b8dba71c0ad54135e84ebbd4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Fourteen laws, one loop: fold(region, f) — the points that refine a region, gathered at the coordinate where they\nlie, and one local reading of the origins met there. Nine were written by the simulation (encounter, disagreement,\nindependence, refinement, history, vacuity, cone, transmission, and the group-by itself); these five are the ones\nthat lived as separate code — authority, roles, payment, verification and retraction.\n\nThe falsifier is a law that needs an edge table to compute. None of the five does: the prefix is the edge."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e9edb946e4861612e6403ae03cefbde04817fe12fe41797ac32dc8c7a98b67f9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:e9edb946e4861612e6403ae03cefbde04817fe12fe41797ac32dc8c7a98b67f9 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Every form is a lattice, and its meet is where two demands agree: the tighter band on a scale, the shared tokens of\nan alphabet, the overlap of two intervals. A meet with no value left in it is not inhabited: the demands conflict.\nIt got its own file because three vocabularies of form had grown with a meet each and only two had a join."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ea259f0f3f7286181b68b4079bd17ba0ea51a4e26829572c2387957b513eccb4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ea259f0f3f7286181b68b4079bd17ba0ea51a4e26829572c2387957b513eccb4 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="Two hundred cells, two origins each at random phases; a budget of looks, each adding one origin along the cell's resultant.\nWeight one on the share of pairs that cancel against a choice blind to it: the cells that close, laminar where they were not."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:eaf5b7791d72eaa9f3832f8e91e714baa179954cbcea71c3a2bc45e13a49c02d by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:eb3e39c0f2334de64f01f5e1c1a0f1c93540abe983e8c6fc5becf4634e4a7476 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|brief|cases
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:eb3e39c0f2334de64f01f5e1c1a0f1c93540abe983e8c6fc5becf4634e4a7476 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The falsifier: encounters that land independently of the density already there. Then the ratio does not rise with the epochs and the cells touched grow with the budget, which is what the blind placement in the yes sample shows."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:eb3e39c0f2334de64f01f5e1c1a0f1c93540abe983e8c6fc5becf4634e4a7476 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/brief value="encounters land blind to density"
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ec28fffe029d4f21625c3f2bb0fd7615598d2f035f1ce9583449db7bb2f0bf22 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=said/fields value=about|cases|coverage
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:ec28fffe029d4f21625c3f2bb0fd7615598d2f035f1ce9583449db7bb2f0bf22 by=reader:95297fcf0823 form=alphabet measure=text role=reads scope=said/about value="The size of a body of claims is how many questions it asks: distinct coordinates, never lines. Many lines at one\ncoordinate are one question, and read at a coarser resolution questions merge."
bound-lock/1 at=place:sha256:efe5255a02f1e9781fd342583c72c6e2a8840ec31a405bf7c6e84b50e5b42778 by=reader:76e1db421edb form=alphabet measure=id role=reads scope=source/calls value=Math|by|freedom
